14:["$","div","1",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-7","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full border border-accent/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-accent","children":"Landing Page Load"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted font-medium","children":["Leak ",2]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Slow Mobile Load Time"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 rounded-lg bg-bg p-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-fg-muted mb-1","children":"Signal"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg","children":"Normal CTR, high exit rate (particularly on mobile), mobile conversion significantly below desktop"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted text-sm","children":"A visitor who abandons while the page is loading is recorded as a bounce before they saw your headline. Portent's 2022 analysis of over 100 million page views found that pages loading in 1 second convert at roughly 3× the rate of pages loading in 5 seconds for B2B lead generation. Google's Core Web Vitals define LCP over 4 seconds as 'Poor.' The Chrome UX Report consistently shows LCP scores 40–60% worse on mobile than desktop for the same URL - because mobile devices have less processing power and are often on slower networks."}],["$","details",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fg-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":"Why this causes the loss ↓"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted pl-2 border-l border-border","children":"Landing Page Experience - one of Quality Score's three components - includes page load speed. A poor mobile LCP receives a 'Below Average' rating, raising CPC for mobile-originated traffic. The fix improves both conversion rate and Quality Score simultaneously."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg bg-accent/5 border border-accent/20 p-4 mb-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Run Google PageSpeed Insights (pagespeed.web.dev) on the mobile preset. Identify the LCP element - almost always the hero image. Convert it to WebP or AVIF format (40–60% file size reduction), add a correct `sizes` attribute so mobile devices download a smaller version, and add `fetchpriority=\"high\"` to hint early loading. Defer non-critical scripts and remove unused third-party tools that block rendering. Target: LCP under the Good threshold on mobile."}]]}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-load-time-slow","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"LCP benchmarks and detailed fix guide →"}]]}]
15:["$","div","2",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-7","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full border border-accent/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-accent","children":"Above Fold"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted font-medium","children":["Leak ",3]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-fg","children":"No Proof Before the CTA"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 rounded-lg bg-bg p-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-fg-muted mb-1","children":"Signal"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg","children":"Good page engagement (over 30 seconds average), low form starts or add-to-cart rate"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted text-sm","children":"The visitor read the page but was not convinced. Asking for commitment - an email, a purchase, a demo - before providing evidence that the offer is credible forces the visitor to decide with no supporting data. Cold paid traffic has no prior relationship with the brand. A CTA that appears before any proof signals is asking for trust that has not been earned."}],["$","details",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fg-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":"Why this causes the loss ↓"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted pl-2 border-l border-border","children":"Proof before CTA is a sequencing principle, not a design opinion. The visitor's hesitation peak is immediately before the first meaningful ask. A proof element placed at that moment - a specific testimonial, an outcome stat, a recognisable logo - reduces the cognitive cost of clicking by creating a micro-commitment before the macro one."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg bg-accent/5 border border-accent/20 p-4 mb-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Add one specific, attributed proof element above the primary CTA. A stat with context (\"Used by X operators to identify the exact section killing their conversions\") or a named testimonial with a result (\"Booked 3 new clients in 30 days - Sarah L., Performance Marketing Manager\") placed directly above the button is sufficient. Generic \"5-star rated\" claims without context do not count as proof."}]]}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/proof-before-cta","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"Proof placement guide and 3 no-redesign implementations →"}]]}]
16:["$","div","3",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-7","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full border border-accent/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-accent","children":"Form / Checkout"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted font-medium","children":["Leak ",4]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-fg","children":"High-Friction Form"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 rounded-lg bg-bg p-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-fg-muted mb-1","children":"Signal"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg","children":"Form views but low submission rate (under 20% of form views completing)"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted text-sm","children":"Every additional form field reduces completion rate. Phone number, company size, job title, and budget fields are the most common high-friction additions. Each optional field sends a signal: \"we want more from you than the minimum required to deliver the next step.\" The visitor interprets this as a sales process they did not sign up for and abandons."}],["$","details",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fg-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":"Why this causes the loss ↓"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted pl-2 border-l border-border","children":"Form friction is the most actionable conversion lever on the page because it requires no creative judgment - you either ask for the field or you do not. The principle is: collect only the information required to deliver the immediate next step. Everything else can be collected later in the process, after the visitor has agreed to engage."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg bg-accent/5 border border-accent/20 p-4 mb-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Remove every field that is not required to deliver the next step. For a lead capture form where the next step is sending an email, you need one field: email. For a booking form where the next step is scheduling a call, you need name, email, and phone. 'Company size,' 'how did you hear about us,' and 'message' fields are optional - remove them from the primary conversion form. Collect them post-conversion if you need them."}]]}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-not-converting","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"Landing page conversion diagnosis guide →"}]]}]
17:["$","div","4",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-7","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full border border-accent/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-accent","children":"Mobile Layout"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted font-medium","children":["Leak ",5]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Mobile Friction"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 rounded-lg bg-bg p-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-fg-muted mb-1","children":"Signal"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg","children":"Desktop converts at 3–5%, mobile converts at under 1% on the same page with similar traffic quality"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted text-sm","children":"The majority of paid social traffic arrives on mobile. Broken layouts, full-size images not compressed for mobile networks, CTAs pushed below the fold by oversized hero sections, and tap targets under 44px silently filter out the majority of paid social visitors. The desktop conversion rate masks the mobile failure in blended analytics."}],["$","details",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fg-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":"Why this causes the loss ↓"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted pl-2 border-l border-border","children":"Most landing pages are designed and tested on desktop. The mobile experience is treated as an afterthought - a responsive breakpoint that 'should work.' In practice, the 390px viewport on a real phone reveals failures that DevTools device emulation does not: actual touch interaction precision, real 4G network conditions, and the physical reality of reading a screen that fits in one hand."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg bg-accent/5 border border-accent/20 p-4 mb-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Open the page on a real phone. Read the headline aloud. Is the CTA visible without scrolling? Can you tap every button on the first try with your thumb? Run PageSpeed Insights mobile. Check that LCP is within the Good threshold (under 2.5s). Fix in order: layout visibility, tap targets, load time. Do not rely on DevTools 'mobile view' for this audit - use a real device."}]]}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/mobile-landing-page-leaks","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"Full mobile leak audit: 5 leaks and fixes →"}]]}]
18:["$","div","5",{"className":"rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-7","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-3 mb-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"rounded-full border border-accent/30 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-accent","children":"Trust Signals"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-xs text-fg-muted font-medium","children":["Leak ",6]}]]}],["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Missing Compliance and Trust"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-4 rounded-lg bg-bg p-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-fg-muted mb-1","children":"Signal"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm text-fg","children":"Ad disapprovals, \"Below Average\" Landing Page Experience in Quality Score, low Quality Score on complaint-sensitive keywords"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted text-sm","children":"Google and Meta evaluate trust signals on your landing page when reviewing ads. Missing privacy policy, no physical address or business identification, absent or buried refund/cancellation policy, and no SSL are all trust failures that can trigger ad disapprovals or \"Below Average\" Landing Page Experience ratings. Beyond ad platform compliance, these missing signals erode visitor trust at the payment or commitment stage."}],["$","details",null,{"className":"mb-4","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"cursor-pointer text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-fg-muted hover:text-accent transition-colors","children":"Why this causes the loss ↓"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted pl-2 border-l border-border","children":"Ad platforms disapprove pages that do not meet their landing page policies. Google requires that the landing page URL be accessible, match the display URL, not contain misleading content, and not require users to download software to view it. Beyond policy, visitors making a purchase or committing personal information look for standard trust signals - security badge, recognisable payment methods, clear return policy - in the same way they look for proof of competence."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-lg bg-accent/5 border border-accent/20 p-4 mb-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent mb-1","children":"Fix"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Audit your footer and checkout page: privacy policy link, physical address or business name, email contact, and refund/cancellation terms must all be present and accessible from the landing page. Add SSL if not already present (most platforms include this). Add a trust badge row near any conversion element: payment icons, security seal, guarantee text. Run your ad destination URL through Google's Ad Preview and Policy Checker to identify any active policy flags."}]]}],["$","$L10",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/landing-page-not-converting","className":"text-sm font-semibold text-accent hover:text-fg transition-colors","children":"Full landing page conversion diagnosis →"}]]}]
19:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-5 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Quick-triage table: what you see → where to look"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","div","High CTR, high bounce, under 15s on page",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg text-sm","children":"High CTR, high bounce, under 15s on page"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-accent font-medium mt-0.5","children":"Leak 1 (message-match) or Leak 2 (load time)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mt-1","children":"Check mobile LCP first, then H1 vs ad headline"}]]}],["$","div","High CTR, high bounce, 15–45s on page",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg text-sm","children":"High CTR, high bounce, 15–45s on page"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-accent font-medium mt-0.5","children":"Leak 3 (no proof before CTA)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mt-1","children":"Check what proof element is visible before the first CTA"}]]}],["$","div","Low CTR (under 3%) on search",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg text-sm","children":"Low CTR (under 3%) on search"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-accent font-medium mt-0.5","children":"Ad layer - not a page problem yet"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mt-1","children":"Fix ad copy or keyword match types before the page"}]]}],["$","div","Mobile bounce 20+ points above desktop",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg text-sm","children":"Mobile bounce 20+ points above desktop"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-accent font-medium mt-0.5","children":"Leak 5 (mobile friction)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mt-1","children":"Open the page on a real phone and run mobile PageSpeed"}]]}],["$","div","Form views but low submissions",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg text-sm","children":"Form views but low submissions"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-accent font-medium mt-0.5","children":"Leak 4 (form friction)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mt-1","children":"Count form fields - remove anything not required to deliver the next step"}]]}],["$","div","Ad disapprovals or low Quality Score",{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg text-sm","children":"Ad disapprovals or low Quality Score"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs text-accent font-medium mt-0.5","children":"Leak 6 (trust signals)"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-muted mt-1","children":"Check footer for privacy policy, address, refund terms; run Google's Ad Policy Checker"}]]}]]}]]}]
1a:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-6 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Frequently asked questions"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div","0",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"Where does most paid traffic get lost before converting?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"In the pages Nebula audits, the most frequently failing signals appear on the landing page itself - specifically in the first 5 seconds after arrival. If the landing page headline does not match the ad promise (message-match break), or if the page loads slowly on mobile, the visitor may exit before engaging with any content. A second common failure is the absence of proof before the CTA: the visitor reads the page but sees no evidence that the offer is credible. High bounce rate combined with low time-on-page suggests an arrival-level failure, while page engagement without form starts suggests a trust or CTA signal failure."}]]}],["$","div","1",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"What is the most common reason paid traffic does not convert?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Message-match break between the ad and the landing page is a primary root cause. The ad creates a specific expectation - a keyword, an offer, a tone - and the page does not fulfil it. The visitor arrives, scans the first screen, does not recognise the promise they clicked on, and leaves. This is indicated when CTR on the ad is healthy (above 3-5% for search) but bounce rate on the landing page is above 70% with under 15 seconds time-on-page. Another frequent cause is mobile load time: a visitor who abandons while the page is loading is recorded as a bounce before seeing anything."}]]}],["$","div","2",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How do I identify which stage is leaking my paid traffic?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Work through the leak map in stage order, using analytics signals as candidate indicators: (1) Check ad CTR - if under 3% for high-intent search, the problem is likely the ad, not the page. (2) Check bounce rate and time-on-page for paid traffic - high bounce + under 15 seconds suggests message-match or load time failure. (3) Check mobile vs desktop conversion split - if mobile is 50%+ lower, evaluate mobile layout or mobile LCP. (4) Check form starts vs form submissions - if visitors start but do not complete forms, form friction is indicated. (5) Check checkout abandonment rate - if add-to-cart rate is healthy but purchase rate is low, evaluate checkout friction. Use the earliest failing stage to prioritize testing."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"border-b border-border pb-6 last:border-0 last:pb-0","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 font-semibold text-fg","children":"How long does it take to fix a paid traffic conversion leak?"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Depends on the leak. Message-match fixes - rewriting the headline to mirror the ad - can be live in under an hour. Mobile LCP fixes - converting the hero image to WebP and adding correct sizing attributes - typically take 2–4 hours including testing. Form friction fixes - removing optional fields - take under an hour. Layout fixes for mobile - implementing a sticky CTA bar or restructuring the above-fold section - typically take 4–8 hours of development time. The most time-consuming fix is trust signal work - gathering, formatting, and placing new testimonials or case study content. The $97 One-Leak Repair Sprint targets the highest-priority failing signal, delivers the exact fix for you or your developer to implement, and includes a 30-day re-audit to verify the condition changed."}]]}],"$L26"]}]]}]
